WEBVTT

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:09.510
Good morning, Akiho-san.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.050
Good morning, Kaito-san.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.040
How would you like your breakfast eggs?

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.900
I'd like them scrambled today.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.030
And fluffy?

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:24.780
Yes, fluffy!

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.580
Did you sleep well?

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:28.740
Yes!

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:32.490
Oh, but... I had that dream again.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:33.530
Again?

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:39.100
I'm standing somewhere up high,

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:41.720
looking down at someone.

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:48.140
I still can't tell who it is,

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.280
but there's something I want badly...

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.370
And I realized last night that, 
since I'm watching that person,

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.930
they must have that thing.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.670
When you told me about the dream before,

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:03.690
you said you weren't sure why you 
were looking at this person.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.910
Yes, but today, I knew for sure.

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.590
I was thinking, "I want that thing you have."

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:17.830
Perhaps your dream is gradually progressing.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.680
Progressing?

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.860
But I still can't do anything in it.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:26.190
But your consciousness is progressing.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:31.560
This time, you realized why you 
were there, did you not?

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:34.100
Yes, that's true...

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:39.680
Does that mean I'll figure out 
who it is I'm looking at, too?

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:47.200
I'm sure of it.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:53.580
<b>Sakura and the Icy Ball-Sports Tournament</b>

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.960
Why didn't you wake me up?

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.400
I just woke up myself.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.480
I set an alarm, too...

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.670
Oh, yeah, you turned it off.

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:09.380
Like this... "Unnngh!"

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.100
So you <i>were</i> awake!

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.400
Nah, I was half asleep.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.260
I wanted to sleep a little longer...

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:17.550
I still had one meat bun left!

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.470
But if I'd gone back to sleep, 
the baseball game would've started...

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.600
Oh, the hair clip Yukito-san gave me...

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:22.390
Here.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.100
My pen case!

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:23.950
Here!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:24.900
Handkerchief and towel!

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.030
Here!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:26.770
Gym clothes!

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:28.990
Here ya go-go!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:31.700
All set...

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.970
All thanks to my support.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:37.400
Sakura-san, breakfast is ready.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.050
Dad?

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:42.260
Morning, Sakura-san. Did you oversleep?

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:42.760
Morning.

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:48.380
Yeah, I did... but I thought you 
weren't coming home today?

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.260
I wasn't, but there were some reference 
materials here I wanted to check.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.760
I wanted to see you and Toya-kun, too.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.690
Get the juice out of the fridge, would you?

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:01.630
Sure.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:05.940
Huh?

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.270
Where's Onii-chan?

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:09.670
He's working this morning.

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:12.620
He ate before he left, though.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.650
I should have gotten up early, too.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.840
Let's eat!

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:25.280
<i>I could have spent more time with Dad...</i>

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:30.350
Sorry I'm away all the time, lately.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.040
That's okay. You have work.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.850
Besides, you seem to enjoy it.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.200
Do I?

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.890
Yeah! Did you find something good?

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:42.770
I'm excited since we might find something 
really valuable this time.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.240
I'm rooting for you!

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.100
Thanks. I'll do my best.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.870
By the way, this friend you wanted 
to show our books downstairs to...

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.760
Right, Akiho-chan.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:56.690
Toya-kun cleaned up a bit, 
so you can go down anytime.

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:00.530
I hope I'll be home when she comes over...

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:03.600
I hope I can introduce you! 
She's really nice!

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.120
I'm glad you've made such a great friend.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:09.680
Yeah! You know, at school today, she'll be—

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.250
Oh! School!

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:18.260
Even as a middle schooler, 
some things never change...

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.270
<b>Will you be okay?</b>

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.260
Thanks for breakfast!

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.870
Bye!

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.240
Have a good day.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:36.050
Some things about her still 
make her seem like a child,

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:40.320
and some things make her seem so grown-up...

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.670
But she's really grown into 
a wonderful young lady.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:48.040
Keep watching over her, Nadeshiko-san.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:57.150
For all your worryin' that you'd be late, 
you sure chowed down at breakfast.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.320
It's been a long time since 
I got to eat with Dad.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:02.020
Plus, it was really good!

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:04.910
Lucky! What'd you eat?

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:05.780
Mini Hamburg steaks.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.000
Lucky!

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.280
Syaoran-kun!

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:14.650
Oh, it's just him.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:17.680
Morning!

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:19.230
Morning. Let's hurry.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:19.910
Yeah.

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:24.680
It's unusual to see you leave so late.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:27.660
Yeah, Wei called as I was leaving,

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.360
and we kind of got to talking.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.770
How is Wei-san doing?

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:33.750
He's fine.

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:37.680
He was worried about whether 
I was doing okay on my own.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.290
He did stay with you last time, huh?

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:40.930
Yeah.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:44.510
Bet he's worried 'cause he knows 
you're still so immature...

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.020
Probably.

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:51.380
We should hurry, or we'll really be late.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:52.140
Yeah.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:56.780
Morning!

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:58.360
Safe!

00:07:58.360 --> 00:07:59.480
Thank goodness.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:00.850
Good morning.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:01.740
Morning!

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:08.250
Good morning. Everyone take your seats.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:13.860
It's been a long time since I saw 
you slide in at the last second.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.330
That was too close...

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:17.770
I hope Syaoran-kun made it in time.

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:19.600
He was with you?

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:20.260
Yep.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:22.370
An early morning date!

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:24.930
Nah, Sakura just overslept.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:26.220
Kero-chan!

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:29.760
S-Sorry...

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:34.220
Now, we have our ball-sports 
tournament, today, starting in third period.

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:39.030
Everyone, have a good time together, 
and try not to get hurt.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.120
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:42.600
Chiharu-chan, aren't you playing volleyball?

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.040
Yeah. How about you?

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:44.820
Basketball!

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:47.150
Isn't it exciting?

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:49.850
I can't wait to see you play!

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:51.740
I hope the weather stays clear.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.510
The forecast said it would.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.050
That's good, but...

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:58.590
What's wrong?

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:03.980
Students can't shoot video 
during the tournament.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:05.840
What a shame...

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:07.970
You wanted to film it?

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:21.460
I'm right here, ain't I?

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:37.140
Great job!

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:44.370
As usual... You "thought this might happen"!

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:48.360
So you brought a spare camera. 
I knew you would, Tomoyo!

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:54.510
Here!

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:02.840
Way to go!

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:07.200
I do wish I could film everyone else 
to make it more exciting to watch,

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:10.480
but I doubt Tomoyo would want that.

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:26.850
Class 1-2 wins!

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:32.570
You were awesome!

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:33.430
Good game!

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:34.570
How'd yours go?

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.360
We won!

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:37.770
You were wonderful!

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.730
Only because everyone else was amazing.

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.110
What's up?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.620
Akiho-chan!

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:57.690
Syaoran-kun?

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:00.660
Yep. Akiho-chan is up against Li-kun.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:01.610
Oh, my!

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.750
They're both so good.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:16.490
I knew Li-kun was pretty athletic,

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:18.340
but Akiho-chan is amazing, too.

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:21.140
She did say she liked tennis,

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:23.400
but I guess she's good at badminton, as well.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:39.030
Whoa! She's pretty amazing, 
hitting a shot he couldn't return!

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.290
Right. Sakura, Sakura...

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.270
What are they playing to?

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:57.400
First to 21 points wins.

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.660
<i>I want to cheer for both of them!</i>

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:19.160
<i>But I really want both of them to win.</i>

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:24.690
<i>I wonder if a tie would be possible.</i>

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:42.350
Everyone, get inside!

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:44.190
Inside the building!

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.750
We need to get inside, too!

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:47.700
Right...

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.340
Hurry!

00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:50.360
R-Right!

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.240
Let's go!

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:52.900
Yeah.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:00.700
Sakura-chan?

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.160
This is...

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:24.280
For now, they're asking everyone 
to wait until the hail stops.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.210
Syaoran-kun, do you need to 
be with the committee?

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:28.730
I asked Yamazaki to handle it.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.240
Besides, this is more important now.

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:33.500
It looks like this hail

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:36.660
really is only falling around 
Tomoeda Middle School.

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:39.780
All the teachers were bewildered.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:41.250
It's gotta be...

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:45.910
A card...

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:50.310
In that case, Sakura-chan, take this!

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:54.430
I thought this might happen,

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.860
so I made sure to waterproof it!

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:00.360
First the camera, now the outfits...

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.910
You really impress me, Tomoyo.

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.120
You flatter me.

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.210
You look lovely!

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:14.710
I can't use the drone to film 
you in this hail, though...

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:17.000
Well, in its place,

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:20.450
I'll just use my wings and my super 
mobility to get the perfect—

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:21.600
Watch out!

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:25.710
Sakura!

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:32.630
<i>Reflect!</i>

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:35.100
All right!

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:38.060
The school building!

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:39.730
<i>Reflect!</i>

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:45.500
Just hitting it back will wreck the school!

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.070
There's gotta be a way.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:50.700
It's fallin' like crazy now!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:53.690
Hail is ice, so the thing 
to fight it with is...

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.290
Something hot!

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:56.400
Fire.

00:14:57.990 --> 00:14:59.350
Th-There aren't any...

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:02.500
We don't have a single fire-based card!

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:14.380
Go get 'em, kid!

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:16.340
<i>Fire god, come forth!</i>

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:28.200
Why?

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:31.630
I guess this spell won't work anymore...

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:33.440
Sakura!

00:15:58.770 --> 00:15:59.980
Wow.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:10.930
Sakura!

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:11.640
Right.

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:14.100
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:17.660
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:19.930
<i>Secure!</i>

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:40.930
"Hail"...

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.060
<b>Hail</b>

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.320
Um...

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:45.050
Sakura!

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:47.560
Sakura-chan, are you all right?

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:50.640
I'm fine. What about you? Are you okay?

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:51.610
Yes.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:52.940
And you, Syaoran-kun?

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:01.630
Syaoran-kun?

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:04.070
Someone's comin'!

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:18.290
Sakura-san! Tomoyo-san! Li-kun!

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:21.000
So this is where you were.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:24.250
I thought you'd be taking shelter 
from the hail, somewhere.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.970
We've been looking for...

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:30.280
Sorry we worried you. We're totally fine.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:33.330
Akiho-chan?

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:37.160
Sakura-san, your outfit...

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:41.400
U-Um, well... You see, Akiho-chan...

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:44.900
Th-This is, um... uh...

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.430
Uh...

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:49.030
It looks beautiful! It's for 
another play, right?

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:49.850
Huh?

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:51.790
U-Uh...

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.420
What kind of play will it be?

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:55.970
Oh, that's right!

00:17:55.970 --> 00:18:01.300
You must show me the video of the one 
in which you played a princess, too!

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:07.660
<i>Can't you just lend her 
the video of that play?</i>

00:18:08.010 --> 00:18:09.840
I'm too embarrassed...

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:11.780
<i>But it was so cute!</i>

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:16.150
<i>That hail must've given you 
a rough time, though.</i>

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:18.730
<i>So there wasn't any where you were?</i>

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:19.990
No, it was clear all day.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:23.870
Sorry, I couldn't do anything to help.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.000
Oh, no!

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:30.120
Just letting me talk to you 
about it helps a lot!

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:33.020
<i>Thanks.</i>

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:35.660
<i>By the way, is Toya home yet?</i>

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:39.760
No, he sent a message saying 
he'd be a little late.

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:44.900
<i>He had to work longer to cover 
for someone who had a cold.</i>

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:48.970
I'm always telling him not to 
push himself too hard...

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:52.150
Would you tell him that for me, too? 
Pound it into his head!

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:53.220
<i>Pound it?</i>

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:56.760
He's always convinced that he's 
tough enough to handle it.

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:59.160
But when he does get a fever, 
he can barely get rid of it.

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:02.100
Okay. I'll pound it into his head.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:05.930
But I think it'd be more 
effective if you did it.

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.820
<i>He doesn't listen to me at all!</i>

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:11.990
<i>He's always so mean!</i>

00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:15.920
<i>Just the other day, 
he actually made konjac rice!</i>

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:15.190
That isn't really true.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:18.770
<i>Anyway, about reading to the kids...</i>

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:19.980
Yes?

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:24.190
<i>The others said they'd be thrilled
 if you'd come to help.</i>

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:26.590
I can't wait!

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:27.400
<i>Same here.</i>

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:31.770
<i>Well, you must be tired. Get some rest, okay?</i>

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.720
You, too. Goodnight.

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:36.830
<i>Goodnight, Sakura-chan.</i>

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:49.190
<i>For once, he came home and went 
straight to bed, even without dinner.</i>

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:53.450
<i>He's really been sleeping a lot, lately.</i>

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:59.990
It's early, but I guess I'll go to bed, too.

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:11.720
Goodnight, Kero-chan.

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:29.710
This dream again?

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:43.610
The sound of clocks...

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.720
So you <i>do</i> want my key?

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:15.470
Why?!

00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:26.960
I don't know why I got this 
key in my dream, either!

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:29.640
Do you know?

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:33.890
Who are you?!

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:51.340
Why?

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:53.160
Because...

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:54.810
Why?

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:56.130
Because...

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:59.280
Because...

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:12.200
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:14.540
Are y'all gettin' your exercise?

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:20.350
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:20.350
<b>K</b>

00:24:14.540 --> 00:24:16.760
It's the smart, athletic segment, 
"Leave It to Kero-chan!"

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:20.800
Today, we're looking at... yet 
another battle costume!

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:21.350
<b>Make one for me, too!</b>

00:24:21.350 --> 00:24:24.250
This one's a poncho type that's 
easy to put on and take off,

00:24:24.250 --> 00:24:27.960
the perfect choice when disaster 
struck the ball-sports tournament.

00:24:27.960 --> 00:24:32.060
The wing pattern on the back is 
perfect for Sakura, ain't it?

00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>K</b>

00:24:32.060 --> 00:24:34.120
And Akiho's amazing at badminton.

00:24:34.120 --> 00:24:35.390
I was so fascinated by her,

00:24:35.390 --> 00:24:38.360
I didn't get much of Sakura on video, 
but don't tell Tomoyo...

00:24:38.360 --> 00:24:39.990
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:41.870
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.350 --> 00:24:42.630
Meiling-chan's visiting from Hong Kong.

00:24:42.630 --> 00:24:45.490
I was surprised to see her, but I'm so happy!

00:24:45.920 --> 00:24:48.830
Not only that, but she'll 
be staying at my house.

00:24:49.120 --> 00:24:51.630
Next time, "Sakura and 
Welcome Back, Meiling."

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura and Welcome Back, Meiling</b>

00:24:51.940 --> 00:24:55.010
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
